course: dictionary
lesson: 12238
title: Consist: made up of
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a word is made of smaller parts, the word «consist» tells you what those parts are. «A week consists of seven days.» This means a week is made up of seven days. The days are the parts, and «consists of» introduces them.
explain: The words after «of» are the parts. «The mixture consists of salt and water.» Look at what comes after «of»: salt and water. Those are the things the mixture is made from.
explain: In a more formal sentence, «consist in» means that something is the main or only part of a thing. «Her skill consists in patience» means that patience is the main part of her skill.
fact: Consist is a verb. Its forms are consist, consists, consisted and consisting.
fact: Use «consists» for one thing, as in «A week consists of seven days.» Use «consist» for more than one thing, as in «The buttons consist of plastic.»
fact: «Consist of» means to be made up of certain parts or things.
fact: «Consist in» is a formal phrase. It means to have something as the main or only part.
fact: In maths, a problem may say what a whole consists of. Find the parts listed after «of» to solve it.
exercise: «A week consists of seven days.» What does consists of mean here? | Starts on a Monday | Is bigger than | Is the same as | *Is made up of
exercise: Complete the sentence: «The mixture ___ salt and water.» | consist of, all at once | consisting of | *consists of | consisted of yesterday
exercise: «The team consists of five players.» How many players are in the team? | Four | Ten | *Five | Some
test: «My lunch consists of soup and bread.» What is in my lunch? | *Soup and bread | A sandwich only | Cake and tea | Nothing at all
test: Pick the right form: «Yesterday, the cake ___ flour, eggs and sugar.» | consisting of | consist of | consists of | *consisted of
exam: Complete the sentence: «Her skill ___ patience.» (formal, meaning patience is the main part) | *consists in | consists to | consists with | consists of
